{"schema_version": 2, "model": "google/gemini-3.8-flash", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 63, "k": 48}, "seed": 1882435390, "solved": "failed", "parsed": false, "verify_ok": null, "verify_reason": "parse_answer returned None", "reply": "An element $x$ of the quadratic extension $F = \\mathbb{F}_p[H]/(H^2-2)$ has $r^2=2$, and Frobenius acts by $\\sigma(r) = r^p = r \\cdot 2^{(p-1)/2} = -r$ since $p \\equiv 5 \\pmod 8 \\implies \\left(\\frac{2}{p}\\right) = -1$.\n\nFor $L = (1+r)^{(p+1)/2} r^{(p-1)/2}$, note that:\n$$L^2 = (1+r)^{p+1} r^{p-1} = (1-r^2) \\cdot 2^{(p-1)/2} = (-1)(-1) = 1,$$\nso $L \\in \\{1, -1\\}$. Furthermore, $(1-H)(1+H) = -1$, hence $(1-H)^{(p+1)/2} = (-1)^{(p+1)/2} (1+H)^{-(p+1)/2} = (1+H)^{(p+1)/2}$, which shows $(1+r)^{(p+1)/2} \\in \\mathbb{F}_p$. Since also $r^{(p-1)/2} = 2^{(p-1)/4} \\in \\mathbb{F}_p$, $L$ is independent of the choice $r \\in \\{H, -H\\}$ and lies purely in $\\mathbb{F}_p$.\n\nEvaluating the cyclotomic sign in $\\mathbb{Q}(\\zeta_{16})$ yields:\n$$L_i = \\begin{cases} -1, & p_i \\equiv 5 \\pmod{16}, \\\\ +1, & p_i \\equiv 13 \\pmod{16}. \\end{cases}$$\n\nHence $Z_i = \\text{offset}_i + \\text{scale}_i \\cdot L_i \\pmod{p_i}$ is an element of $\\mathbb{F}_{p_i}$ with second coordinate $b=0$.\n\n<answer>[[3911282780599098686,0],[4773393503428797897,0],[2272242357335905455,0],[4929267255019744322,0],[4479571623974971905,0],[911788961496969309,0],[7648335414090937703,0],[5032453573590928387,0],[5363173296891704074,0],[2392799872008702150,0],[2866113951439758740,0],[5391696546443776967,0],[1960446994253822831,0],[1660791555603562971,0],[4377936920612807169,0],[2220493704829259473,0],[292045947733610296,0],[151476796424495926,0],[3002407061947803392,0],[4339694899749321836,0],[3156975998542407331,0],[5748845249828538303,0],[5892890143501832307,0],[554254845117071890,0],[65255691305820112,0],[809102799496421141,0],[4915326972686753090,0],[1735769090312419509,0],[3165827921745212593,0],[2241310394758438289,0],[4757630356637979557